  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;DELTA UPSILON FRATERNITY HOUSE (ANN ARBOR, MICHIGAN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Delta Upsilon Fraternity House (Ann Arbor, Michigan) is a fraternity house located at 1331 Hill Street in Ann Arbor, Michigan, and was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1995."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DELTA UPSILON FRATERNITY HOUSE (CHAMPAIGN, ILLINOIS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Delta Upsilon Fraternity House (Champaign, Illinois) is a historic fraternity house located at the University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign in Champaign, Illinois, built in 1926-27 for the university's chapter of the Delta Upsilon fraternity, which was established in 1905."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DELTA UPSILON FRATERNITY HOUSE (AMES, IOWA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Delta Upsilon Fraternity House (Ames, Iowa) is a historic building located in Ames, Iowa, United States, designed by Des Moines architect Alexander M. Linn, who joined Delta Upsilon at what was then called Iowa State College."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAMS COLLEGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Williams College is the founding institution of the Delta Upsilon fraternity, where it was established in 1834."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF MICHIGAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Michigan is the location of the Delta Upsilon chapter founded in 1874."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF ILLINOIS AT URBANA–CHAMPAIGN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign is the location of the Delta Upsilon chapter established in 1905."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IOWA STATE UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iowa State University is the current name of the institution where Alexander M. Linn joined Delta Upsilon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Iowa State University is the location of the Delta Upsilon chapter house designed by Alexander M. Linn."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALBERT KAHN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Albert Kahn was a Detroit architect who designed the Delta Upsilon Fraternity House in Ann Arbor, Michigan, in 1902-1903."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEONARD STEUBE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leonard Steube was the architect who designed the Tudor Revival building for the Delta Upsilon Fraternity House in Champaign, Illinois, in 1926-27."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALEXANDER M. LINN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alexander M. Linn was a Des Moines architect who designed the Delta Upsilon Chapter House in Ames, Iowa, in 1930."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEORGE CHANDLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"George Chandler was an early member of the Delta Upsilon fraternity at the University of Illinois, known for his academic success."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARNOLD BECKMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arnold Beckman was an early member of the Delta Upsilon fraternity at the University of Illinois, known for his academic success."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DELTA UPSILON INTERNATIONAL FRATERNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Delta Upsilon International Fraternity is the global organization of the Delta Upsilon fraternity."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DELTA UPSILON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Delta Upsilon is a fraternity founded in 1834 at Williams College in Williamstown, Massachusetts, with chapters at multiple universities."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAMSTOWN, MASSACHUSETTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Williamstown, Massachusetts is the location where the Delta Upsilon fraternity was founded in 1834."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IOWA STATE COLLEGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iowa State College is the former name of Iowa State University, where Alexander M. Linn joined Delta Upsilon."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DES MOINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Des Moines is the city where Alexander M. Linn practiced as an architect before designing the Delta Upsilon Chapter House."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TUDOR REVIVAL ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tudor Revival architecture is the style of the Delta Upsilon Fraternity House in Champaign, Illinois, designed by Leonard Steube."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMPOSITE PHOTOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Composite photos are used to decorate the walls of fraternity houses, often featuring members from past years."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PADDLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paddles are decorative items often used to decorate fraternity houses, sometimes with historical significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECRET SOCIETIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Secret societies, including fraternities and sororities, have unique traditions and practices."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRATERNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fraternity is a type of social organization, often found on college campuses, with specific rituals and traditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SORORITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sorority is a type of social organization, often found on college campuses, with specific rituals and traditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IOWA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Iowa is the state where the Delta Upsilon Chapter House in Ames, Iowa, is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ILLINOIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Illinois is the state where the Delta Upsilon Fraternity Houses in Champaign and Urbana are located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICHIGAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Michigan is the state where the Delta Upsilon Fraternity House in Ann Arbor is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;URBANA–CHAMPAIGN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urbana–Champaign is the combined name for the University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL REGISTER OF HISTORIC PLACES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The National Register of Historic Places is a list of buildings, sites, structures, objects, and districts deemed worthy of preservation."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRST CONTACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"First contact refers to the initial communication or interaction between the fraternity and the outside world, symbolized by the establishment of the fraternity house."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACADEMIC SUCCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Academic success is a characteristic of the early members of the Delta Upsilon fraternity, including George Chandler and Arnold Beckman."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALUMNI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alumni are former members of the fraternity who contribute to the fraternity's success through donations and support."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HILL STREET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hill Street is the street where the Delta Upsilon Fraternity House in Ann Arbor, Michigan, is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYLAND AVENUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hyland Avenue is the street where the Delta Upsilon Chapter House in Ames, Iowa, was originally located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREAT AND CO.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treat and Co. published the Cyclopædia of Fraternities, which includes information about the Delta Upsilon fraternity."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CENTURY MAGAZINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Century Magazine published an article about college fraternities, which includes information about the Delta Upsilon fraternity."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE HARVARD CRIMSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PUBLICATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Harvard Crimson published an article about secret societies in colleges, which includes information about the Delta Upsilon fraternity."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0492-52e21b748576</data>
    </node>
